; 128K: music player entry points
;
; Three entry points that load the registers for #R$85C2 and call a routine of the music player in the music bank. The
; 128K code is not disassembled and was not run (the simulator is a 48K machine), so what each call does is a guess
; from the callers: Unknown. The names are the callers' names.
; .
; #R$85E8: DE = $FC4B, HL as the caller left it; called by #R$887B at the end of the ending (the stub at $88D5 that
; #R$605F turns into CALL $85E8). Probably silences the music.
; .
; #R$85EE: HL = $CA8A, then as #R$85F3; called through the stub at #R$A31E when SPACE is held on the title (the info
; screen).
; .
; #R$85F3: HL = $C09D, DE = $F9D7; called through the stub at #R$860C when a game starts and by #R$A31E when SPACE is
; released. Probably starts the module at HL (the music is a Vortex Tracker II module).
; .
; Hardware: 128K paging port, through #R$85C2.
@label=MusicEntryEnding
c$85E8 LD DE,$FC4B          ; music bank routine at $FC4B
 $85EB JP $85C2
@label=MusicEntryInfo
 $85EE LD HL,$CA8A          ; module address for the info screen (assumed)
 $85F1 JR $85F6             ; skip the next LD HL
@label=MusicEntryGame
 $85F3 LD HL,$C09D          ; module address of the game music (assumed)
@label=MusicCallF9D7
*$85F6 LD DE,$F9D7          ; music bank routine at $F9D7
 $85F9 JP $85C2
